Day 1 - Cohort - DevOps & GIT & GITHUB


DevOps
=====

Development + Operations 

Before DevOps => Waterfall methodology -> Agile methodology

Waterfall is best when requirements are fixed and predictability matters.
Agile shines when customer needs evolve and rapid iteration is key.
DevOps extends Agile by automating delivery and bridging Dev + Ops for speed and reliability.

Waterfall methodology Flow (Documentation & Planning)
===================================
Requirements -> Analysis -> Design -> Coding -> Testing -> Operations

Agile methodology Flow (Customer collaboration)
==============================
Plan -> Design -> Develop -> Test -> Deploy -> Review -> Launch

DevOps Methodology Flow (Automation & Integration) 
=================================


Push code -> Build -> Test -> Deployment (Dev/Tst/Ldt/Uat) -> Approval -> Deploy (PRD)

Continuous Integration		- Push code + Build + Test
Continuous Delivery		- staging /pre-prod Deploy
Continuous Deployment 	- Approval + PROD deployment

SAST - Static Application Security Testing
- Code-level issues
- Prevent vulnerabilities
- during coding
DAST - Dynamic Application Security Testing
- Runtime vulnerabilities
- Validate exploitability
- during testing

